-Use`-recover_power` to specify the percent of paths with positive slack which
-will be considered for gate resizing to save power. It is recommended that
-this option be used with global routing based parasitics.
+Use `-recover_power` to specify the effort (0–100) for power recovery using
+available slack headroom (positive slack when the design is closed, otherwise
+slack above the current worst slack). The resizer performs multi-pass recovery that
+greedily reduces power using available timing margin by (when safe) removing
+redundant non-clock buffers, downsizing standard cells (including clock network
+cells), and (when multiple VT types are available) swapping to lower-leakage VT
+variants. Recovery preserves setup/hold timing closure by not pushing setup/hold
+WNS below 0 when the design is closed. When setup timing is already failing
+(WNS < 0), recovery may allow a small additional setup WNS degradation budget
+(by default 2% of the minimum clock period, scaled by the `-recover_power`
+effort) to trade performance for power. It also avoids increasing max
+slew/capacitance/fanout violation counts. It is recommended that this option be
+used with global or detailed routing based parasitics.
 
 #### Instance Name Prefixes
 
